    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0049" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/688</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Adviser on Political
                        Relations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-03">October 3, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador of Chile informed me that he had been instructed by his Government
                    to state that it would be very glad to accept the armament set forth in the
                    lists recently furnished the Ambassador in the event that Chile ruptures
                    diplomatic relations with the Axis. The Ambassador made special mention of the
                    fifty planes which the President had offered in addition to the equipment on the
                    lists furnished him by the Department.</p>
            </div>
